AUDIO: '[music] &gt;&gt; All right, YouTube. What is good? It\'s your boy Rebel back with another video. And today, we are taking a look at Mr. Flow. So, Mr. Flow is a training-free stage sampling method for accelerating a'

[00:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'trained flow matching text-to-image diffusion models. Mr. Flow first samples a low-resolution image, upsamples the decoded result in pixel space with real-ESRGAN, re-encodes the upsampled'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image, injects scheduler-consistent low-strength noise, and performs a short high-resolution refinement. The pipeline shifts most denoising cost from expensive high-resolution sampling to cheaper low-resolution sampling while'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'preserving local detail quality. So, essentially, the way that this model works is it generates an image at almost full step count at a low resolution being 512 by 512. And then, it takes the latent and upscales it in pixel space'

[00:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with real-ESRGAN upscaler, then decodes and passes to your finished output. The result is a low resolution brought into a high resolution space for less compute'

[01:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and faster gen times. This works with distilled models, guffs, int 8, cavrats, everything you can think of. This is going to run with. And this version, which is the original contributors Mr.'

